ty-gate single-owner + backfill\n\n**done-when:** Each curation carries a verified/documented/lossy badge from an evidence-iterating loop, no path produces unearned pass, the badge shows in the briefing + Helping Hand, and the shadow-run diff meets the promotion gate.\n\n- **Given** a candidate with disagreeing critics, **when** the fix-loop runs, **then** it expands the evidence corpus deterministically and re-scores, never re-prompting critics to pass\n- **Given** a candidate that fails to converge within MAX_EVIDENCE_ITERS, **when** the loop exits, **then** the verdict is force-downgraded to flag (never pass)\n- **Given** a validated candidate, **when** the briefing or Helping Hand renders it, **then** its verified/documented/lossy badge and incorporation note are shown\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Trustworthy cost numbers\n\n**Intent:** Make the cost ledger reflect real spend (the $118 incident class).\n\n**Deliverables:** Replace the UNVERIFIED pricing.yaml guesses with real Google/Anthropic SKU rates; Meter the MCP server query-embedding path (server.py:_embed_query), currently unmetered; Regression test asserting the model tag used at call time matches a pricing.yaml key\n\n**Depends on:** Evidence-rigor fix-loop and confidence badge\n\n**done-when:** Every LLM call is metered against a pricing.yaml key that matches the model tag used at call time, verified by a regression test.\n\n- **Given** a nightly run, **when** costs roll up, **then** every callâ€™s model tag resolves to a pricing.yaml key (no $0 fiction), asserted by a regression test\n- **Given** a Helping Hand query, **when** it embeds the query, **then** the embedding call is metered into the costs table\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Scout memory and source-reputation\n\n**Intent:** Give the discovery swarm memory â€” prioritize high-yield sources while still exploring new ones; surface source quality (Johnâ€™s addition; down-payment on the learning loop).\n\n**Deliverables:** Per-source yield tracking (which sources produced accepted/verified artifacts vs noise); Explore/exploit seed prioritization respecting the existing 2-curator + 3-night-shadow promotion rule; Source-quality indicator per artifact in the library + briefing\n\n**Depends on:** Trustworthy cost numbers\n\n**done-when:** Scout passes prioritize historically high-yield sources, spend a measurable budget on new exploration, and each artifact shows a source-quality indicator.\n\n- **Given** N nights of yield history, **when** a sweep plans its scout pass, **then** high-yield sources are prioritized and a measurable exploration budget is allocated to new sources\n- **Given** an artifact, **when** the library or briefing renders it, **then** a source-quality indicator is shown\n","numLines":83,"startLine":1,"totalLines":83}}}
