ml` guesses with real SKU rates, meter the MCP query-embedding path, add a regression test tying call-time model tags to pricing keys (the \"$118 incident\" class).\n- **W5 â€” Scout memory + source-reputation:** per-source yield tracking, explore/exploit seed prioritization (respecting the 2-curator + 3-night-shadow rule), and a per-artifact source-quality indicator.\n\n### Execution outcomes (all dated 2026-06-06, branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`)\n- **All 5 waves converged GREEN** in order via EXECUTEâ†’ADVERSARIAL-REVIEWâ†’FIXâ†’RE-REVIEW, each with 2 independent adversarial reviewers.\n- **Test gate rose monotonically:** 684 baseline â†’ 690 (W1) â†’ 700 (W2) â†’ 724 (W3) â†’ 735 (W4) â†’ **750 passed** (+66 total). No test weakening; security suite green throughout.\n- **W1:** new `briefing_delivery.py` (session note + best-effort Windows toast); `library/index.md` regenerated to 540 placeable rows / 1 unplaced (99.8% â‰¥ 95% target).\n- **W2:** servable SQL literal now lives only in `gate.py`; live-DB backfill â†’ 0/889 NULL (all `clean-with-notes`).\n- **W3:** `roles/evidence.py` + `roles/shadow_diff.py`; loop runs in SHADOW (live verdict unchanged, zero added LLM cost); migration 0022 applied.\n- **W4:** `pricing.yaml` gains a `verification:` provenance block; `_embed_query` now metered; `tests/test_pricing_keys.py` added.\n- **W5:** `roles/source_reputation.py`; explore/exploit ordering wired into scout fan-out; migration 0023 applied.\n- **Commits:** 148cf10 (baseline) Â· 828f3f9 Â· 5c32bb6 Â· 0bde41a Â· b997d65 Â· 87e2192 â€” **not pushed, awaiting John's review.**\n- **Out-of-scope honored:** no parallel judgment fan-out, no WAL write-actor, no Foreman-durability checkpoints; serial loops stand.\n\n### Open tripwires / accepted residual risk (carried forward)\n- **W2:** the served-text backfill marks artifacts servable from name+short_description only, not payload â€” a malicious-payload/benign-description artifact is servable in enforce mode. Do not treat enforce mode as production-trustworthy until a payload-depth scan supersedes it.\n- **W3:** production binding derives the badge from pre-computed critics; true per-iteration LLM re-scoring is a promotion-gated upgrade, enabled once the shadow diff meets the gate.\n- **W4:** opt-in alt providers (openai/xai/mistral) lack pricing keys â€” they record visible $0 + a one-time warning until rates are added.\n- **W5:** yield history is 0 today (existing sources predate `seed_id`); it accrues going forward with no fake backfill, and budget-capped exploration is opt-in.\n\n---\nNote: there are several other `foreman-handoff-*` folders (phase2, quality, dashboard, awareness). I summarized the base `foreman-handoff/` because its title and member-document names (\"Aurora Revamp â€” Implementation Plan / Execution Log\") match exactly. Tell me if you meant a different one."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6893,"cache_read_input_tokens":33789,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6893},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13895e3b-9099-4f07-8852-bcbf02c58a68","uuid":"97e9c767-905b-487b-8b32-1f90c5d18099","request_id":"req_011Cc1HjvMUBLKKJkn7Re1ZC"}
